o slide on the floor as a result of downwards vertical velocity if `stop_on_slopes` is set to `false`.\r\n\r\nFixes [83673](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83673)\r\n\r\nThe change is very small, as the issue was that `stop_on_slopes` was simply not being used at all when handling sliding on slopes.\r\n\r\nTODO:\r\n -Check if the same problem exist in 2D and implement the same fix.\r\n\r\n\r\nPre PR:\r\n`stop_on_slopes` has no effect at all on stopping on slopes.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc359830-1c53-4d86-9ad1-58cdc8664da1\r\n\r\n\r\nPost PR:\r\n\r\nThe character slides as expected.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5571e19d-b4db-4b31-9a2b-fd3dec76b62a\r\n\r\nNOTES:\r\n\r\nQ: Why the character was sliding a super tiny bit if we didn't had the functionality in the first place?\r\nA: Because `p_cancel_sliding` is used wrong in various places (Similar case to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99397),  I hope to address that soon.\r\n\r\nMPR:\r\n\r\n[stop_on_slopes_fix.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17926939/stop_on_slopes_fix.zip)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2024-11-26T23:58:38Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T23:22:21Z","closed_at":"2024-12-10T20:41:19Z","merged_at":null,"mer